config ATM_VENDOR_DFU
	bool "Atmosic vendor-protocol DFU helper"
	depends on FLASH
	depends on FLASH_MAP
	help
	  Shared DFU helper consumed by vendor OTA protocols (Samsung TagSDK,
	  Apple FMNA UARP, ...) so each vendor port can call a single uniform
	  API without having to know the local MCUboot / partition layout.

	  Behaviour is selected at compile time from devicetree:

	    * If both slot1_partition and slot3_partition exist, the helper
	      runs in dual-image mode: a 32-byte "ATMX" header at the start
	      of the stream selects the per-image sizes, Image 0 is routed
	      to slot1_partition and Image 1 to slot3_partition. The combined
	      binary is produced offline by scripts/pack_combined_image.py.

	    * If only slot1_partition exists, the helper runs in single-image
	      mode: incoming bytes are streamed directly into slot1_partition
	      with no header parsing.

	    * If slot1_partition is missing, every API call returns -ENOTSUP
	      with a warning so vendor protocols built without MCUboot still
	      link and run cleanly.

	  When CONFIG_MCUBOOT_BOOTLOADER_MODE_SWAP_USING_OFFSET is enabled,
	  the helper shifts each slot write by the first sector size so
	  MCUboot can accept the secondary-slot images. Upgrade requests are
	  forwarded to MCUboot via boot_request_upgrade_multi() when
	  CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER is enabled, and otherwise return
	  -ENOSYS.

if ATM_VENDOR_DFU

module = ATM_VENDOR_DFU
module-str = atm_vendor_dfu
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ATM_VENDOR_DFU
